tle": "NH governor race: Ayotte maintains lead over Warmington in new poll", "source": "WMUR", "published": "2026-10-22T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxObktIRjZBdlRMaXhIaVltNTQyQkRDRmZ0OU5CLTd3NUJ5VHg5ejRpWVZrUVRUQVFFamF6ZUJLRnVFaGtuYUFqUWh5UVZsRU5ZTEFvRUVRYlBXUjBmMDdxNjR4ZUM2UXJXVTI1cVpPRlRMUlVFbVRPbW91c1VPbVVpekNWdWJxQQ?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": -4.28, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": -5.53, "poll_sd": 4.7, "poll_weight": 0.56, "fundamentals": {"margin": 1.85, "lean": 1.5, "environment": 4.35, "incumbency": -4.0, "money": 0.0}, "rating_margin": -8.38, "sigma_race": 5.0, "sigma_total": 5.41, "baseline_margin": -4.99, "analyst_adjustment": 0.49, "key_factors": ["Incumbent Kelly Ayotte leads in nearly all polls, averaging about five points", "Final UNH poll shows the race deadlocked at 48-48, suggesting late tightening", "Expert ratings cluster at Likely/Lean R, with one Solid R", "Ayotte draws Democratic ticket-splitters in a state leaning Democratic federally"], "rationale": "The polling average puts Ayotte ahead by roughly five points, and most raters call the race Likely or Lean R, but the final high-quality UNH survey shows a tie, so the forecast sits slightly better for Warmington than the average. Incumbency and her crossover appeal keep Ayotte favored.", "watch": "Whether the late tightening in the UNH poll is real or an outlier; another independent final poll or strong Democratic turnout in federal races could narrow this further.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Kelly Ayotte (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Governor Kelly Ayotte seeks a second term against Democrat Cinde Warmington in a state that leans slightly Democratic on the ballot but has a history of splitting tickets. Polling through late October consistently showed Ayotte ahead, with Republican-sponsored surveys giving her larger leads and independent pollsters closer margins. The final University of New Hampshire survey, however, showed the race deadlocked at 48-48 even as Democrats led in federal and legislative contests on the same ballot.\n\nExpert raters mostly place the race in the Likely or Lean Republican column, and prediction markets price Ayotte as a strong favorite. Ticket-splitting appears central: some voters backing Democrats federally plan to keep Ayotte, whose approval has held up despite the state's lean. Warmington has campaigned hard and drawn national surrogates, but she needs to consolidate Democratic voters who have been crossing over.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -8.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0698, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0784, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1135, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0954, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0873, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0914, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1036, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0759, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0785, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0513, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0304, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0619, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.044, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.0422, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.0653, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.0661, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "202